{
 "design": "Collaboration prediction v4: learn link prediction on the WHOLE co-author graph, then score faculty pairs.\n\nWhy: the faculty-only data has ~100-250 new links a year. The full co-author graph of the verified corpus (faculty + all their co-authors,\n~17k people) has ~350-600 new links a year among pairs that are two steps apart, so ~4x more training positives.\n\nProtocol (strictly temporal, one-year-ahead, same faculty test pairs as v3):\n  snapshot T: graph of papers up to T; label = the pair co-authors a paper in T+1 and had never done so before\n  fold test_T: train on snapshots T' <= test_T - 1, test on faculty-faculty never-collaborated pairs at test_T (label = year test_T + 1)\n  folds 2020..2024; headline = 2024 (label 2025); predictions of the 5 folds are also pooled (rank-normalised inside each fold)\nModels (all LightGBM):\n  A  faculty-only data, v2 features                  (= the v3 LightGBM, the reference)\n  B  structural features from the big graph, trained on faculty pairs + all other author pairs (the new idea)\n  C  same structural features, trained on faculty pairs only (ablation: does the extra data matter, or just the features?)\n  A+B, A+C rank averages",
 "params": {
  "A": {
   "n": 200,
   "lr": 0.03,
   "leaves": 7,
   "mcs": 30,
   "spw": 10
  },
  "B_and_C": {
   "n": 300,
   "lr": 0.03,
   "leaves": 7,
   "mcs": 100,
   "spw": 1
  }
 },
